  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nWhen building a web component, it isn’t currently possible to use a select element inside the shadow root and let the web component user provide option elements to be slotted into the select. Here’s an example:\n```html\n<my-custom-select>\n  <template shadowrootmode=open>\n    <select>\n      <slot></slot>\n    </select>\n  </template>\n  <option>one</option>\n  <option>two</option>\n</my-custom-select>\n```\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nIf I wanted to build this today, I'd create a MutationObserver to detect changes to the custom element's subtree and clone the options into the shadow root. I'm not sure how I'd deal with copying the styles from the options.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nI would solve this by changing the select element to look for options in its flat tree.",
